I deployed the example frontend application as a Docker container to Render (render.com).

The source code is in my GitHub repository https://github.com/Zanaad/docker in the
directory example-frontend. I created a Web Service on Render, connected it to that
repository and selected Docker as the runtime, with example-frontend as the root
directory. Render builds the image from the Dockerfile in that directory: the first
stage installs the npm packages and builds the static React files with npm run build,
and the second stage serves the build folder with the npm package serve on port 5000.
Render detects the port, runs the container and gives the app a public https URL.

Only the frontend is deployed, so the buttons that need the backend do not work,
but the page itself is served from the container in the cloud.
